## Session Start

1. Read `IDENTITY.md`. That is layer 0 and it is the map of this workspace.
2. Find your task in the Routing table above. If no row fits, ask before improvising one.
3. Open the job card at that destination and read its Inputs table.
4. Load exactly what the Inputs table names, at the scope it names. Nothing else. Loading more does not make the output better.
5. Pull only the rule books the job card lists, from `_config/`.
6. Do the work. Write to the locations in the job card's Outputs table.
7. Close against the job card, then append the line to `_log/LOOP-LEDGER.md`.

## Rule Books

`_config/` holds the rule books. A rule book is reference material: it says what is true and what is allowed here. It never says what to do next, and it is never called a skill. Pull one only when a job card names it.

| Rule book | Holds | Pulled when |
|---|---|---|
| `_config/conventions.md` | naming, folder layout, file shapes, layer discipline | creating, moving or renaming any file |
| `_config/glossary.md` | this project's terms and the one meaning each carries | any wording decision, any new term |
| `_config/voice.md` | audience, tone, vocabulary, evidence standard | writing anything a human will read |
| `_config/style.md` | formatting mechanics: headings, tables, links, dates, numbers | writing or editing markdown |
| `_config/{{EXTRA_RULEBOOK}}.md` | {{EXTRA_RULEBOOK_HOLDS}} | {{EXTRA_RULEBOOK_WHEN}} |

Rule books are edited by a human. Agents propose changes into `_log/FORGE-PROPOSALS.md` and wait.

