## Pipeline

<!-- Keep this section only for projects that compile something in stages.
     Stages can be virtual (defined here, no new folders) or physical (a folder per
     stage, each with its own layer 2 job card). Prefer virtual on an existing
     project: do not restructure what already works. -->

The model is a compiler here, not a chatbot. Each stage takes named inputs and writes a named artifact. Conversation belongs at the review gate, not inside a stage.

```
{{STAGE_1}} -> {{STAGE_2}} -> {{STAGE_3}} -> {{STAGE_4}}
```

| Stage | Job card | Reads | Writes |
|---|---|---|---|
| {{STAGE_1}} | `{{STAGE_1_CARD}}` | {{STAGE_1_READS}} | {{STAGE_1_WRITES}} |
| {{STAGE_2}} | `{{STAGE_2_CARD}}` | {{STAGE_2_READS}} | {{STAGE_2_WRITES}} |
| {{STAGE_3}} | `{{STAGE_3_CARD}}` | {{STAGE_3_READS}} | {{STAGE_3_WRITES}} |
| {{STAGE_4}} | `{{STAGE_4_CARD}}` | {{STAGE_4_READS}} | {{STAGE_4_WRITES}} |

A stage hands off through files. Stage N writes to its `output/`, stage N+1 reads from there. A human can open that file, edit it, and the next stage picks up the edit. There is no other state.

{{/PIPELINE}}

